 "cleaning_notes": [
  "Source: supplemental file 1 (one-page PDF table), converted with xpdf pdftotext 4.00 in '-table' mode from a copy of the zip member in SV-G1/out/work/scb516/. The '-layout' mode scrambles the wrapped cells of this table; '-table' keeps each dog's row, with wrapped text (breed, sex, location) on the line above it. Fields were cut at the header column positions.",
  "Supplemental file 2 (differential WBC counts) holds figure panels only; its text is the caption. No values were read from it. Its dog IDs (D1-3 experimental, N1-11 natural) cannot be linked to the '#' numbers of file 1.",
  "One record per dog: the 15 naturally infected dogs, timepoint 'admission' (signs at admission per the article's results; the table gives no sampling time). The 3 experimental dogs of the article are not in file 1.",
  "No laboratory values per dog are in the files (the article's lactate, haematology and biochemistry results are group summaries only).",
  "Neutral dog_id from the table number '#'. The table is sorted by outcome (#1-8 died, #9-15 survived), so the original number carries the label; it is only in the outcomes file.",
  "Age: text such as '6Y 11 Mo' converted to months (years x 12 + months).",
  "Sex and neuter status from one cell: 'male gelded' and 'female neutered' -> neuter 'neutered'; 'intact' -> 'intact'. Neuter status is missing (null) for 2 dogs whose cell gives only the sex.",
  "travel_location: the 'assumed location of infection based on travel history' as written; 'no travel history (Switzerland)' is stored as 'Switzerland (no travel history)'. travel_abroad = 1 if a foreign country is named.",
  "Clinical signs are 0/1 as in the table (caption: 0 absent, 1 present). Lethargy and pale mucous membranes are present in all 15 dogs and carry no information.",
  "Fever flag against body temperature: highest temperature with fever 0 is 38.6 degC, lowest with fever 1 is 39.1 degC; the threshold is not stated (inferred to lie between them). The flag is consistent with temp_c in every dog.",
  "Severity labels and the features: the label here is death, not a complication score, so no clinical-sign column defines it. Note that icterus, pigmenturia (haemoglobinuria) and epistaxis (bleeding) appear as complications in other severity definitions (e.g. WHO-style 'complicated' babesiosis in S-CB017); they are kept as features and analysts using a complication-based label elsewhere should not treat them as independent of it.",
  "Death: 8 dogs labelled 'Died' in file 1. The article says 6 died spontaneously within 24 h of admission and 2 were euthanised within 48 h for clinical deterioration; which 2 is not in the files. 'died' therefore includes euthanasia.",
  "All dogs received imidocarb (3-6 mg/kg IM, some with doxycycline) after admission sampling per the article; not in the file.",
  "Raw header typos ('Fieber', 'temeprature') are kept in the 'original' fields; the age typo 'Mio' is flagged below.",
  "FLAG: S-CB516:d002: age written '4 Y 8 Mio' ('Mio' read as months, Mo)"
 ]
}
